 "result_text": "`git machete github checkout-pr` now says `PR #N is already closed in repository org/repo` when the PR exists but is closed. If the PR doesn't exist, it still says \"is not found\". I haven't run it or the tests, so the change is untested.\n\nWhen the PR isn't in the open list, `checkout_github_prs` (in `git_machete/client.py`) now asks GitHub for that single PR by number. I added a helper in `git_machete/github.py`, `is_pull_request_closed`, to do that lookup.\n\nIf that lookup itself fails, the helper treats the PR as not closed. A missing PR (404), an auth problem or a network error all fall back to the old \"not found\" message. That means a failed lookup on a private repo will still say \"not found\" rather than surfacing the underlying error.\n\nMerged PRs count as closed, because GitHub reports their state as `closed`. The message doesn't distinguish merged from closed-without-merging.",
